mittee","when":"2022-02-11T00:00:00","desc":"Majority required","type":"Adopt Item as Amended","result":"Carried, 8-0","yes":8,"no":0,"votes":[["Ana Bailão","Yes"],["Denzil Minnan-Wong","Yes"],["Gary Crawford","Yes"],["James Pasternak","Yes"],["Jennifer McKelvie","Yes"],["John Tory","Yes"],["Michael Thompson","Yes"],["Paul Ainslie","Yes"]]}],"text":["At its meeting on February 7, 2022, the Budget Committee considered Item BU45.1 headed \"2022 Capital and Operating Budgets \" and made recommendations to the Executive Committee. The Executive Committee will make recommendations on the 2022 Capital and Operating Budgets to City Council for its consideration at its meeting on February 17, 2022.","City Council on February 17, 2022, adopted the following: 2022 Operating Budget COMMUNITY AND SOCIAL SERVICES Children's Services 1. City Council approve the 2022 Operating Budget for Children's Services of $671.877 million gross, $579.584 million revenue and $92.293 million net for the following services: Service : Gross Expenditures($000s) Revenue ($000s) Net Expenditures ($000s) Child Care Delivery 468,260.3 407,717.4 60,542.9 Child Care Service Management 203,616.3 171,866.3 31,750.1 Total Program Budget 671,876.6 579,583.7 92,292.9 2. City Council approve the 2022 staff complement for Children's Services of 1,051.2 positions all of which are operating positions. 3. City Council continue to urge the Province of Ontario and the Government of Canada to sign an agreement regarding the Canada-Wide Early Learning and Child Care Plan, and City Council request the General Manager,…"],"sourceId":"2022.EX30.2","sourceUrl":"https://secure.toronto.ca/council/agenda-item.do?item=2022.EX30.2","sourceName":"Toronto TMMIS — agenda item","sourceUrlBasis":"pattern","verificationStatus":"pattern-verified"}